;; si's check programs (bin/si check; doc/scheme/SCHEME-SURVEY.md, "As built: SM5 (write-ahead)", "As built: SCS3"): the run
;; programs of Racket's R6RS suite (:suite: judged by their own report alone, test by test, SCS3; their libraries found through
;; the library path .tmp/si/suite-lib, tests -> the corpus; :tests the count of tests the report must give, so that a run that
;; stops early with status 0 fails: the suite's own count, as si's and Chez's reports gave it when SCS3 recorded it, the same),
;; Larceny's R6RS programs (with their input files on stdin) and si's own programs (test/scheme/si/programs/): :golden their
;; expected stdout, Arbace's own, reviewed against R6RS and si's design (doc/scheme/SCHEME-SURVEY.md, "As built: SCS3" for si's,
;; "As built: SCS6" for Larceny's, SCS6 (b)), :status the exit status (default 0) and, when not 0, :error the kind of the
;; error its first stderr line names (arbace.scheme.check/error-of); Chez's recorded runs (test/scheme/si/ref-chez.edn) are
;; bin/si own's, by hand, no judge's. :file is relative to the fetched corpora (:corpus) or the checkout. SCS8 (b): Larceny's two
;; benchmarks run as their authors meant: :libraries-first, the file's leading library forms put on the library path by the harness
;; (arbace.scheme.check/split-libraries, Larceny's layout) and the program after them run; :own-input, an input of our own (the
;; checkout's; :input, the corpus's); :bench, judged by the benchmark's own result check (the name run-benchmark prints, and no
;; "Error: Benchmark program returned wrong result"; arbace.scheme.check/bench-items). SCS11 (b): the same two at the corpus's own sizes
;; (its earley.input, 1000 iterations; nboyer.input, problem size 5: 51,507,739 rewrites), :aot-only: run at the compiled level alone
;; (bin/si check --aot, the night's si-aot; interpreted they would take hours), judged by the same result checks.
